&lt;h3&gt;Building Movements vs. Moments&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Any organization can capitalize on a moment—a flashpoint in the news cycle with enough of a connection to an organization’s mission to spark a quick, short-term increase in donations, sales, etc. Far more difficult is the process of creating a &lt;em&gt;movement&lt;/em&gt;—a sustained, long-term effort on the part of your organization and its audience to make change, leading to lasting results.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
